pay as you go:
->easily adapted to changing the business needs
->improve responsiveness to change
->adapt based on needs ,not forecast
example-> let says you are running 10 instance
and later you do not want 5 instance so now you can only pays for 5 services.

save when you reserve:
->invest in reserved capacity (egs: RDS AND EC2).let say for some years.
->saves up to 75% as compared to on-premise (pay-as-you-go).

6 advantages of AWS cloud computing:

1:trade capital
2:benefits from massive economies of scale
3:stop guessing capacity(what really needed)
4:increase speed and agility
speed=(deploy resource easily and quickly)
