high availability in aws:
is the measurement of :
the amount of time data is available to access
expressed as a percentage of time per years
eg:99.99

->designed for no single point of failure(acheived through data redundancy)
->synchronous & asynchronous replication
->lower cost as compared to fault tolerence(ft)
->service that creates HA:
	Elastic Load Balancing
	EC2 auto scaling
	amazon route 53(dns service



vs fault tolerenc:
->no service interruption
->no downtime
->synchronous replication
->higher costing
->server are:
	fault tolerenc nic
	disk mirroring(RAID-1)
	synchronous db replication
	redundant power



durability:
is the protection against
->data loss
->data corruption
->s3 with 11 9's3
(99.999999999)
